# Principal divisors on the level-N modular function field over L

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.hasPrincipalDivisors_laurentBaseChange_modularFunctionFieldFull`
(`8ebe6701-822e-59da-ada6-f1e842929172`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `4482b742-e52e-5fc5-a0f0-53e2ebb1b589`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, let $N \geq 1$ be a natural
number, and assume `ModularPolynomialFamily`: for every prime $\ell$ there is a
`ModularPolynomialData` $\ell$, that is a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ with $\Phi$ of degree
`dedekindPsi` $\ell$ in its outer variable and $\Phi$ vanishing at `evalAtJ` and `jqN` $\ell$, whose
$\Phi$ in addition satisfies `EvalSymm`, i.e. for all Laurent series $x, y$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ the
two evaluations $\Phi(x,y)$ and $\Phi(y,x)$ obtained by substituting into inner and outer variable
agree. Consider the intermediate field `laurentBaseChange L (modularFunctionFieldFull N)`: the
$L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map induced by
$\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the expansions
$\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(jq)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. The conclusion is that
this field $F$ has `HasPrincipalDivisors` over $L$: for every $f \in F$ with $f \neq 0$ there is a
finitely supported function $D$ from the places of $F/L$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing the
image of $L$, distinct from $F$ itself, and principal ideal rings) to $\mathbb{Z}$ with $D(v) =
v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $v$ and with $\sum_v D(v)\,\deg(v) = 0$.

This is the statement that a nonzero function in the function field of $X_0(N)$ over $L$, realised
through $q$-expansions, has a divisor of degree zero, with only finitely many zeros and poles. It
supplies the principal-divisors hypothesis required by the divisor class group of this field, and is
used by the unconditional form of the same assertion and by the corresponding statement for
`modularFunctionFieldBar`.

